  pen:{kicker:'Late delivery and refunds', title:'When a contractor misses a deadline, and how money comes back', intro:'Every milestone carries an agreed date. Tarmem tracks it against the evidence the contractor submits. Missing it has a fixed, published cost, so both sides know the consequence before the work starts.',
    ladderTitle:'Late-delivery ladder', ladderSub:'Per project. A strike is recorded when a milestone is 3 or more days past its agreed date without evidence submitted.',
    ladder:[{n:'1',fee:'SAR 500',t:'First missed deadline',d:'A SAR 500 late fee is deducted from the contractor’s next release and credited to the homeowner’s project balance.'},{n:'2',fee:'SAR 1,500',t:'Second missed deadline',d:'A SAR 1,500 late fee, deducted and credited the same way. The contractor is warned that the next strike ends their control of the project.'},{n:'3',fee:'Homeowner decides',t:'Third missed deadline',d:'The homeowner chooses: continue and give one final chance, or cancel the agreement and take the remaining held amount back in full. Tarmem’s fee on the cancelled balance is waived.'}],
    graceTitle:'What does not count as a strike', grace:['Delay the homeowner caused (access, late approvals, change requests).','Delay agreed in writing inside the project before the date.','Documented force majeure: weather closures, government stoppage, supply recalls.'],
    refundTitle:'Refunds', refundSub:'Money held with the payment provider belongs to the homeowner until a milestone is approved. These rules say when it goes back.',
    refunds:[{h:'Before the work starts',p:'If the project is cancelled before the first milestone is submitted, the full held amount returns to the homeowner within 5 working days. Tarmem’s fee is refunded too.'},{h:'Milestones not started',p:'Money held for any milestone the contractor has not begun is refunded in full on cancellation, whoever cancels.'},{h:'Milestone in progress',p:'Paid pro rata against verified work. Tarmem’s inspector or the two parties agree the percentage; unresolved cases follow the dispute route.'},{h:'Approved milestones',p:'Not refundable through Tarmem. Approval releases the money to the contractor; defects afterwards are a warranty claim against the contractor.'},{h:'Third-strike cancellation',p:'The remaining held amount returns in full, late fees already credited stay with the homeowner, and Tarmem waives its fee on the unspent balance.'},{h:'Timing and method',p:'Refunds go back to the original payment method within 5 working days of approval. Bank transfers may take a further 2–3 days to appear.'}],
    hoTitle:'Third late delivery recorded', strike3:'Third late delivery', stAwait:'Awaiting your decision', hoBody:'has missed three agreed dates. The two late fees (SAR 2,000) are already credited to your balance. Choose how to continue:', hoCont:'Give one final chance', hoContSub:'The contractor gets a new date. A further miss cancels the agreement automatically.', hoCancel:'Cancel and take my money back', hoCancelSub:'Remaining held amount', hoCancelSub2:'returns to you within 5 working days. Tarmem’s fee on it is waived.', hoDone:'Your decision is recorded', hoDoneCont:'Final chance granted. A new milestone date has been requested from the contractor.', hoDoneCancel:'Agreement cancelled. Refund request', hoDoneCancel2:'is approved and will reach your original payment method within 5 working days.', confirm:'Confirm', back:'Back'},
